================================================================================
THM-563 GENERAL BOUNDED-BASE FINITE CHECK -- COMPLETE
mac-mini-2026-06-21-S7, THREAD 1
================================================================================

CLAIM (THREAD 1 deliverable):
  period-max(B) < 15*margin(B)  for ALL primitive bounded bases B subset [0,14],
  0 in B, |B| = k-1, at every k = 8,9,10,11,12,13.
  => Delta_w <= period-max/15 < margin_k  for ALL integer far speeds w >= 15
  => p0(B u {w}) = Plat(B) + Delta_w < cap_k   for all w >= 15  (SINGLE-FAR CLOSED).

DEFINITIONS (canonical):
  Plat(B)   = decorrelated plateau = measS7(B) + p1(B)/7   (whole-circle breakpoint method)
  margin_k  = cap_k - Plat(B)   (skip base if <= 0; NONE occurred)
  period-max(B) = max over one period [0,P), P=7*lcm(B), of  w*Delta_w
              = max_w  sum over one-miss sector-j arcs (j,a,b) of [Sc_j(w*b)-Sc_j(w*a)]  (THM-563 id)
  Sc_j      = centered sawtooth, |S_j| <= 3/49, range R_j = 6/49.
  caps      = cap_8..13 = 2243/5880, 1979/4004, 55/91, 66/91, 6/7, 1  (canonical / orchestrator).

METHOD (two-stage, ALL candidates exact-verified in Fractions):
  STAGE A (a-priori, no scan): period-max <= sumR := (6/49)*(#arcs).  If sumR < 15*margin, PASS.
  STAGE B (exact scan): numpy float scan of f(w) over [0,P) via per-endpoint period tiling
     (each Sc_j(frac(w*t)) periodic with period q | 7e <= 98; tile to length P).
     Take all residues within 1e-9 of the float max -> candidates; recompute f in EXACT
     Fractions; period-max = exact max.  Verified: candidate-max == brute-force exact max
     on 15 small-period k=9 bases (0 mismatches).  Consec bases reproduce canon exactly
     (k=8 pm=1, k=9 pm=43/49, k=10 pm=1007/980).

