================================================================================
CONCLUSION
================================================================================
THM-563's general bounded-base finite check is COMPLETE for k=8,9,10,11,12,13.
period-max(B) < 15*margin(B) holds for EVERY primitive bounded base B subset [0,14].
=> The SIGNED single-far case is CLOSED for ALL bounded bases at all binding k, for all
   integer far speeds w >= 15, with NO finite-w window and NO appeal to THM-546's lossy
   (6/49)V absolute bound.

The binding family is the even arithmetic progressions (0,2,...,2(k-1)) = 2*consec_{k-1}
(DILATED consec bases), worst at k=9 with ratio 13.28.  Headroom to 15 is +0.227 there.
This is consistent with THM-563's dilated/continuous section being the tight regime; the
integer period-max (13.28) sits below the threshold, so the dilated case closes too.

NOTE on the trivial-pass ratios up to ~14.999: these are the a-priori sumR/margin ratios,
NOT exact period-max ratios.  A base passes STAGE A iff sumR < 15*margin, which already
GUARANTEES period-max <= sumR < 15*margin -- so the closeness of sumR/margin to 15 for some
trivial bases is harmless (the true period-max is far smaller, as the scanned worst of 13.28
shows).  Every base whose a-priori sumR/margin >= 15 was exact-scanned (STAGE B); all such
bases have exact ratio well below 15 (worst 13.28).
